From: Sangbaek Park <sangbaekpark@chromium.org>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 09:23:59 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [M159] blink/encryptedmedia: Fix UAF in
 MediaKeySession::OnSessionKeysChange

Original change's description:
> blink/encryptedmedia: Fix UAF in MediaKeySession::OnSessionKeysChange
>
> MediaKeys::createSession() checked MediaKeys::GetExecutionContext() but
> constructed MediaKeySession using ExecutionContext::From(script_state)
> (the receiver wrapper's realm). When a MediaKeys V8 wrapper was dropped
> and recreated in another realm (such as a detached iframe's media
> element), MediaKeySession observed an already-destroyed
> ExecutionContext whose ContextDestroyed() never ran.
>
> In addition, MediaKeySession::OnSessionKeysChange() cached the raw
> ukm::UkmRecorder* (owned by Document) before calling
> MediaKeyStatusMap::AddEntry(), which allocates on the Oilpan heap. If
> that allocation triggered GC and finalized an unreferenced Document,
> the subsequent Record(ukm_recorder) call became a heap-use-after-free.
>
> Fix this by:
> 1. Binding MediaKeySession to MediaKeys' own ExecutionContext instead
>    of the receiver wrapper's ScriptState so MediaKeySession shares
>    MediaKeys' lifecycle and cannot observe an already-destroyed
>    context (enforced with CHECK).
> 2. In MediaKeySession::OnSessionKeysChange(), asserting via CHECK that
>    ExecutionContext is live and looking up UkmRecorder after AddEntry()
>    instead of caching a raw pointer across an Oilpan allocation.
> 3. Adding MediaKeySessionTest.CreateSessionUsesMediaKeysExecutionContext
>    covering the detached-iframe wrapper case.
>
